      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the context before improving understandability.Now I understand the test. The actual test logic is simple: \"hello world\" is 11 bytes, and calling `encodeHex(data, 9, 10, true)` (offset=9, length=10) would read past the end of the array (9+10=19 > 11), so `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` is expected.\n\nThe original file has significant clutter: unused imports, unused constants, and unused helper methods unrelated to this test. I'll produce a clean, focused version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file strips all unused imports, constants, and helper methods down to only what the test needs, and adds named constants (`DATA_OFFSET`, `DATA_LEN`) with a Javadoc explaining exactly why the out-of-bounds exception is expected."
